{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1559176-using-aberrant-rules-for-psions-and-vice-versa","id":1559176,"title":"Using Aberrant Rules For Psions, And Vice Versa","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-01T21:19:56-07:00","id":1559176,"title":"Using Aberrant Rules For Psions, And Vice Versa","content":"Something my head was kicking around for a bit (for first edition).<br /> <br /> <u>Psions Using Aberrant Powers</u><br /> <br /> The standard starts with the rules for psiads in the Aberrant Player's Guide. To reflect the narrow focus and greater power afforded to psions with their powers, some adjustments are in order.<br /> <br /> Psions use 15 transformation points (&quot;nova points&quot;) and have the same restrictions on using them as psiads - no Attributes, no Abilities, no Backgrounds, etc.<br /> Psions start with Psi 2 (chargen max 6).<br /> Designations are by Aptitude rather than Aptitude group. Powers within this purview can be raised to up to three (!) dots. Powers outside of it are restricted to one dot. Some psions can even get powers normally restricted from psiads, in particular QK users (in 1e). Disrupt can be learned at three dots by all psions.<br /> <br /> <b>Biokinesis Aptitude</b><br /> <br /> Armor<br /> Bioluminescence<br /> Body Modification (if any ratings ever come up)<br /> Boost (Physical and Social Attributes only)<br /> Claws (no Kinetic Discharge)<br /> Clone<br /> Disorient<br /> Homunculus<br /> Poison<br /> Sensory Shield<br /> Shapeshift<br /> Stun Attack<br /> <br /> <b>Clairsentience Aptitude</b><br /> <br /> Boost (Dexterity, Social, and Mental Attributes only)<br /> Deflect/Redirect<br /> Intuition<br /> Luck<br /> ESP<br /> Premonition<br /> Pretercognition<br /> Quantum Awareness (Psi Awareness, but, you know)<br /> Sensory Shield<br /> <br /> <b>Electrokinesis Aptitude</b><br /> <br /> Bioluminescence<br /> Boost (Mental Attributes only)<br /> Animal/Plant Mastery<br /> Cyberkinesis<br /> Domination (can buy Parasitic Possession Extra but not Telepathic)<br /> Elemental Anima (Electricity, Light, various forms of radiation)<br /> Holo<br /> Immolate (light, electricity, various forms of radiation)<br /> Invisibility (restricted to sight only)<br /> Magnetic Mastery<br /> Psychic Shield<br /> Sensory Shield<br /> Strobe (light)<br /> Stun Attack<br /> Transmit (electrical and radiation means only)<br /> <br /> <b>Psychokinesis Aptitude</b><br /> <br /> Bounce<br /> Boost (Physical Attributes only)<br /> Claws (must buy Kinetic Discharge)<br /> Deflect/Redirect<br /> Elemental Anima (cold, fire, sound, kinetic energy)<br /> Flight<br /> Force Field<br /> Immobilize (physical only)<br /> Immolate (cold, fire, sound, kinetic energy)<br /> Shroud<br /> Silence<br /> Telekinesis<br /> Weather Manipulation<br /> <br /> <b>Quantakinesis Aptitude</b><br /> <br /> Aberration Transfer (targets others with aberrations)<br /> Absorption<br /> Boost<br /> Density Control (both)<br /> Disimmunize<br /> Matter Chameleon<br /> Momentum Control<br /> Quantum Authority<br /> Quantum Conversion<br /> Quantum Forgery<br /> Quantum Imprint<br /> Quantum Leech (can gain Psi from draining Quantum or Psi)<br /> <br /> <b>Telepathy Aptitude</b><br /> <br /> Animal Mastery<br /> Boost (Mental Attributes only)<br /> Disorient<br /> Domination (must buy Telepathic Extra)<br /> Empathic Manipulation<br /> Hypnosis<br /> Immobilize (vs Willpower only)<br /> Mental Blast<br /> Mirage<br /> Psychic Link<br /> Psychic Shield<br /> Telepathy<br /> <br /> <b>Teleportation Aptitude</b><br /> <br /> Density Control (Decrease)<br /> Disintegration<br /> Disorient<br /> Gravity Control<br /> Spatial Manipulation<br /> Teleport<br /> Warp<br /> <br /> <b>Vitakinesis Aptitude</b><br /> <br /> Biomanipulation<br /> Boost<br /> Disease Authority<br /> Disintegration<br /> Disorient<br /> Entropic Control (biological effects only)<br /> Healing<br /> Immobilize (non-material, vs. Resistance instead of Willpower)<br /> Poison<br /> Sensory Shield<br /> Stun Attack<br /> Temporal Manipulation (only to affect living beings)<br /> <br /> Biotech is still usable under these rules. Consider Biokinetics to have double the Psi for the purposes of formatting tolerance limits.<br /> <br /> <u>Novas Using Psion Rules</u><br /> <br /> Obviously, novas do not have Attunement. Ignore this and biotech.<br /> <br /> Taint: Calculate starting Taint as half the sum of Strength, Manipulation, and Intelligence, somewhat akin to Psi. Each point past 3 gives the nova a mutation from the Trinity core, or an aberration of the appropriate level. If the character has the Taint Resistance merit, she has an effective Taint of half her rating for this purpose. The nova has a pool of Taint points equal to twice her rating. Additional dots of Taint can be bought as Psi.<br /> <br /> Novas can buy up to 30 dots worth of mode effects. She need not obey the typical order in which psions acquire these powers, but each effect has to be bought independently. A mode dot can be exchanged for an Attribute dot or two Ability dots, and novas can increase their Attributes to ratings of up to (5 + Taint).<br /> <br /> Backgrounds can include Dormancy and Eufiber.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}